__pycache__/
*.pyc
service_account.json
*.local.json
.env
.venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SESSION TRANSCRIPTS AND EXPORTS NEVER GO IN GIT.
#
# A transcript holds whatever was discussed: client names, financials, folder
# ids, anything pasted in. The client agreed to Google when they put their files
# in Drive. They never agreed to GitHub, and a client who cannot audit where
# their data went cannot meaningfully consent to it being there.
#
# This is the same category as service_account.json and .env. The repository
# ships the TOOL; the data stays on the machine that made it. Default output is
# ~/.advisor_os/session_exports/, outside any repo, for this reason.
#
# If you ever need to share one, put it in the CLIENT's Drive -- that introduces
# no new party and they can delete it.
transcripts/
session_exports/
*.transcript.md
*.session.md
*.ledger.md
